You absolutely do NOT need to train a model for custom code styles or folder structures — this is a prompt engineering problem, not a model training problem. Here's how to enforce your specific conventions without any retraining:

🧠 Why Fine-Tuning is NOT Needed
Your Goal	Why RAG Works Better
Custom C# naming conventions	❌ Fine-tuning would require 1,000+ examples
✅ RAG injects your rules into prompts (free)
Project folder structure	❌ Training would hardcode paths
